{
  "hero": {
    "titleLine1": "BEHIND",
    "titleLine2": "THE CODE",
    "bioParagraph1": "I never had a CS class in school. My school didn't offer one. But I had a laptop, PC games, and a feeling that the people building this stuff had figured something out I hadn't yet. <span class=\"muted\">I wanted in.</span>",
    "pullQuote": "I can't really stop. I just hit a deadline.",
    "bioParagraph2": "The thing that got me was a fractal simulator I built in Java. Just me, some math I barely understood, and a screen full of something genuinely <span class=\"accent\">beautiful</span> that I made from scratch. That dopamine hit never really left. Building is frustrating and consuming and I wouldn't trade it for anything.",
    "bioParagraph3": "Off the desk I'm probably deep in a cinematic single-player game, ricing my setup for the fourth time this month, or just hanging with people. I like my own space a lot. I also like people a lot. <span class=\"muted\">Both things are true.</span>",
    "photoUrl": "",
    "photoCaption": "burla, 2025"
  },
